IMPORT prelude

-- Civil Service College Act 2001 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a person outside the College: the offences of copying
-- the College's symbol (s 38) or its certificate titles (s 39), the secrecy offence (s 40), composition (s 41), the shield
-- from personal suits (s 16) and the bar on suing to enforce the College's functions (s 13(3)); what the College may award
-- (s 14(1)(d)); and, for those inside it, the Board's size, quorum and voting (ss 5(2), 7(2), 9), the financial year (s 18)
-- and the 2001 transfer of Government employees (ss 31(1), 32(4), 33).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CSCA2001.txt. The deposit says the revised
-- edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the
-- latest amending Act annotated in the text and the Legislative History is Act 5 of 2018 (Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018,
-- s 55, in force 1 April 2018). The ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS at the top of the deposit is out of step with the body for Part 5
-- (it lists s 18 as "Funds of College"); this encoding follows the BODY's numbering (s 18 financial year, s 19 estimates,
-- s 20 funds, s 22 borrowing, s 22A shares, s 23 bank accounts, s 24 application of funds, s 25 investment).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0162 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. Not encoded: incorporation and the seal (ss 3, 4), delegation and committees (ss 6, 8, 11,
-- 12), the functions list beyond s 13(3), the powers beyond s 14(1)(d), the Chief Executive and staff (s 15), the finance
-- provisions other than s 18, the property transfer and existing contracts (ss 30, 34), disciplining pre-transfer misconduct
-- (s 36), regulations (s 42) and the saving (s 43). No regulations made under s 42 were retrieved, so whether ANY offence is
-- prescribed as compoundable under s 41 is not known.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Civil Service College Act 2001 -- the College and the public`

§§ `38 -- the College's symbol`

-- s 38(1): the College "has the exclusive right to the use of any symbol or representation that it may select or devise".
-- (2): "Any person who uses a symbol or representation which -- (a) is identical with that of the College; or (b) so resembles
-- the College's symbol or representation as to deceive or cause confusion, or to be likely to deceive or to cause confusion,
-- shall be guilty of an offence" -- a fine not exceeding $2,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 6 months or both.
-- No intent and no defence is written into s 38(2); nor any exception for use with the College's permission.
GIVEN `uses the symbol or representation` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `identical with the College's` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `resembles it so as to deceive or confuse, or be likely to` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the symbol is an offence` IF
        `uses the symbol or representation`
    AND (    `identical with the College's`
         OR  `resembles it so as to deceive or confuse, or be likely to`)

§§ `39 -- titles of the College's certificates`

-- s 39(1): the College "has the exclusive right in the form and presentation of its titles of certificates and other
-- qualifications". (2): "Any person who issues or uses, or causes or permits the use of, titles of certificates or other
-- qualifications IDENTICAL with those of the College shall be guilty of an offence" -- a fine not exceeding $2,000.
-- Unlike s 38 there is no "so resembles ... as to deceive" limb, and no imprisonment.
GIVEN `issues, uses, or causes or permits the use of, a title` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the title is identical with the College's` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the certificate title is an offence` IF
        `issues, uses, or causes or permits the use of, a title`
    AND `the title is identical with the College's`

§§ `40 -- secrecy`

-- s 40(1): "Except for the purpose of the performance of his or her duties or the exercise of his or her functions or when
-- lawfully required to do so by any court or where required or allowed by any written law, a person who is or has been an
-- officer, employee or agent of the College, a member or a member of a committee of the Board must not disclose any information
-- relating to the affairs of the College, the Board or any other person which has been obtained by him or her in the
-- performance of his or her duties". (2): a fine not exceeding $2,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months or both.
-- The duty survives leaving ("is or has been"). It protects information about "any other person" -- e.g. a course participant.
DECLARE Disclosure HAS
    `the discloser is or was an officer, employee, agent, member or committee member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information was obtained in performing duties or functions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made in performing duties or functions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lawfully required by a court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `required or allowed by written law` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is excepted` IF
        `the disclosure`'s `made in performing duties or functions`
    OR  `the disclosure`'s `lawfully required by a court`
    OR  `the disclosure`'s `required or allowed by written law`

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence` IF
        `the disclosure`'s `the discloser is or was an officer, employee, agent, member or committee member`
    AND `the disclosure`'s `the information was obtained in performing duties or functions`
    AND (NOT (`the disclosure is excepted` `the disclosure`))

§§ `38, 39, 40 -- the penalties`

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `using the College's symbol`
    `using the College's certificate titles`
    `disclosing College information`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS 2000

-- In months; 0 where the section provides a fine only (s 39(2)).
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `using the College's symbol` THEN 6
    WHEN `using the College's certificate titles` THEN 0
    WHEN `disclosing College information` THEN 12

§§ `41 -- composition`

-- s 41(1): "The Chief Executive or any officer authorised by him or her may compound any offence under this Act which is
-- PRESCRIBED as a compoundable offence by collecting from a person reasonably suspected of having committed the offence a sum of
-- money not exceeding $500." (2): "On payment of the sum of money, no further proceedings are to be taken against that person".
GIVEN `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the compounder is the Chief Executive or an authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded for the sum` IF
        `the offence is prescribed as compoundable`
    AND `the compounder is the Chief Executive or an authorised officer`
    AND `the sum` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the sum` AT MOST 500

§§ `16 -- personal suits`

-- s 16: "No suit or other legal proceedings shall lie personally against any officer or employee of the College, member or
-- person acting under the direction of the College, for anything which is in GOOD FAITH done or intended to be done in the
-- execution or purported execution of this Act or any other written law." The College itself can be sued (s 3(a)).
GIVEN `the defendant is an officer, employee, member or person acting under the College's direction` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the act was in execution or purported execution of this Act or other written law` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `done in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a personal suit is barred` IF
        `the defendant is an officer, employee, member or person acting under the College's direction`
    AND `the act was in execution or purported execution of this Act or other written law`
    AND `done in good faith`

§§ `13(3) -- the College's functions are not a duty you can sue on`

-- s 13(3): "Nothing in this section is to be construed as imposing on the College, directly or indirectly, any form of duty or
-- liability enforceable by proceedings before any court."
DECLARE Claim IS ONE OF
    `a claim that the College failed to provide training under section 13`
    `a claim in contract against the College`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 13(3) bars the claim` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a claim that the College failed to provide training under section 13` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `14(1)(d) -- what the College may award`

-- s 14(1)(d): the College may "provide and hold tests and examinations, and grant certificates, awards and other qualifications
-- (OTHER THAN DEGREES), for the attainment of relevant skills, competencies and achievements".
DECLARE Qualification IS ONE OF
    `a certificate`
    `an award`
    `a diploma`
    `a degree`

GIVEN `the qualification` IS A Qualification
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the College may grant it` IF
    CONSIDER `the qualification`
    WHEN `a degree` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§ `Civil Service College Act 2001 -- the Board`

§§ `5(2), 7(2) -- size and resignation`

-- s 5(2): "The Board consists of -- (a) a Chairperson; and (b) not less than 5 but not more than 15 other members, all of whom
-- must be appointed by the Minister." s 7(2): a member "may resign ... at any time by giving not less than one month's notice in
-- writing to the Minister".
GIVEN `other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board is lawfully sized` IF
        `other members` AT LEAST 5
    AND `other members` AT MOST 15

GIVEN `months of notice` IS A NUMBER, `in writing to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the resignation notice is sufficient` IF
        `months of notice` AT LEAST 1
    AND `in writing to the Minister`

§§ `9 -- quorum and voting`

-- s 9(1): "The quorum at every meeting of the Board is the HIGHER of the following: (a) one-third of the total number of members;
-- (b) 3 members." "Member" includes the Chairperson (s 2). The text does not say how a fraction of one-third is treated; this
-- encoding requires the members present to be AT LEAST one-third (so 6 of 16, not 5) -- an inference.
-- (4): questions are "decided by a majority of votes of the members present and voting". (5): the person presiding "has a
-- deliberative vote and, in the case of an equality of votes, he or she also has a casting vote".
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the higher of` MEANS IF `a` GREATER THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `total members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the quorum` MEANS `the higher of` (`total members` DIVIDED BY 3) 3

GIVEN `total members` IS A NUMBER, `members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the meeting is quorate` IF `members present` AT LEAST `the quorum` `total members`

GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `the casting vote is for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the question is carried` IF
    IF `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against` THEN TRUE
    ELSE IF `votes for` EQUALS `votes against` THEN `the casting vote is for`
         ELSE FALSE

§§ `18 -- financial year`

-- s 18: "The financial year of the College begins on 1 April each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year."
-- The function names a financial year by the calendar year in which it begins.
GIVEN `month` IS A NUMBER, `year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the financial year beginning in` MEANS
    IF `month` AT LEAST 4 THEN `year` ELSE `year` MINUS 1

§ `Civil Service College Act 2001 -- the 2001 transfer of Government employees`

§§ `31(1), 33 -- terms on transfer and no abolition benefit`

-- s 31(1): from 1 October 2001 those the Minister determines, employed by the Government in the incorporated departments, "are
-- transferred to the service of the College on terms NO LESS FAVOURABLE than those enjoyed by them immediately prior to their
-- transfer". s 33: despite the Pensions Act 1956, a transferred person "is not entitled to claim any benefit under that Act on
-- the ground that the person has been retired from the service of the Government on account of abolition or reorganisation of
-- office in consequence of the establishment and incorporation of the College". (The s 31(1) "no less favourable" test is quoted
-- here but not encoded: the Act gives no measure for comparing terms.)
GIVEN `transferred under section 31` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `claims abolition or reorganisation of office because the College was established` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 33 bars the pension claim` IF
        `transferred under section 31`
    AND `claims abolition or reorganisation of office because the College was established`

§§ `32(4) -- who pays the pension`

-- s 32(4): the Government "shall be liable to pay to the College such portion of any pension, gratuity or allowance payable to
-- the person on his or her retirement as the same bears to the proportion which the aggregate amount of his or her pensionable
-- emoluments during his or her service with the Government bears to the aggregate amount of his or her pensionable emoluments
-- during his or her service under both the Government and the College". The wording is tangled; this encoding reads it as a
-- pro rata split by pensionable emoluments -- an inference.
GIVEN `the pension` IS A NUMBER, `emoluments with the Government` IS A NUMBER, `emoluments with the College` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Government's share of the pension` MEANS
    `the pension` TIMES `emoluments with the Government`
        DIVIDED BY (`emoluments with the Government` PLUS `emoluments with the College`)
